With a 486 with 8M, try the os/2 version of nethack.  Os/2 lets nethack
use all the memory it need.  There's no 640k to worry about, no strange
concepts called "EMS", "XMS", "UMB" etc.  And you
don't have to install os/2 if you don't want to, it can boot from a floppy.

If you have to use mess-dos, try to "load high" all device drivers & TSRs,
and use some megs as disk cache.  The official msdos version of nethack
don't support xms as far as I know, but you may try an unofficial version
compiled with a dos-extender.

You can put the EMS frame anywhere, as long as it don't overlap with the adresses
used by your expansion cards, or the BIOS.  Check the documentation for
your cards.


